          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The definition of
            %em geodesic convexity
            is like that of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convexity"} convexity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
            generalized to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesics"} geodesics
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_a_riemannian_manifold In a Riemannian manifold
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            and
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset X
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong weakly geodesically convex
                if for any two points from
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                there exists exactly one minimizing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
                in
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                connecting them;
            %li
              %p
                %strong geodesically convex
                if for any two points in
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                there exists exactly one minimizing geodesic in
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                connecting them, and that geodesic arc lies completely in
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                %strong strongly geodesically convex
                if for any two points in
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
                there exists exactly one minimizing geodesic in
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                connecting them, and that geodesic arc lies completely in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                connecting the two points.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong convexity radius
              at a point
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
              (which may be
              = succeed ")" do
                %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} + \infty
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{R}
              such that for all
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \lt r
              the geodesic ball
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_p(r)
              is strongly geodesically convex.
            %p
              The convexity radius of
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
              over the points
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in X
              of the convexity radii at these points.
          %h3#in_a_metric_space In a metric space
          %p
            For
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            %em distance-preserving path
            is a function
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon [a,b]\to X
            which is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometry
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo −
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x(a),x(b)) = b-a
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong geodesic
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em geodesically convex
          %p
            We say that
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %strong length space
            if for any
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
            of the lengths of all continuous paths from
            %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %span.newWikiWord
              Hopf-Rinow theorem
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Hopf-Rinow+theorem"} ?
            says that for a metric space in which every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+subset"} bounded
            subset is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
          %h2#properties Properties
          .un_proposition
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              At any point
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in X
              of a Riemannian manifold, the convexity radius is positive.
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Whitehead"}> Whitehead
            ).
          .un_proposition
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact space
              then the convexity radius of
              %math#mathml_a14fd0f918db282380f1e8f5d0d328c691501375_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
              is positive.
          %p
            This is reproduced for instance as proposition 95 in (
            %a{:href => "#Berger"}> Berger
            )
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+manifold"} paracompact manifold
              admits a complete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
              with bounded absolute sectional curvature and positive injectivity radius.
          %p
            This is shown in (
            %a{:href => "#Greene"}> Greene
            ).
          %h2#references References
          %p Original literature includes
          %ul#Whitehead
            %li
              J. H. C. Whitehead,
              %em Convex regions in the geometry of paths
              Quart. J. Math. 3, 33–42 (1932).
          %ul#Greene
            %li
              R. Greene,
              %em Complete metrics of bounded curvature on noncompact manifolds
              Archiv der Mathematik Volume 31, Number 1 (1978)
          %p A review of geodesic convexity in Riemannian manifolds is in
          %ul#Chavel
            %li
              Isaac Chavel,
              %em Riemannian geometry – A modern introduction
              Cambridge University Press (1993)
          %ul#Berger
            %li
              Marcel Berger,
              %em A panoramic view of Riemannian geometry
          %p A categorical perspective on geodesic convexity for metric spaces can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              %em> Taking categories seriously
              , Reprints in Theory and Applications of Categories, No. 8, 2005, pp. 1–24. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/TAC/reprints/articles/8/tr8.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Much of the issues on geodesic convexity becomes more complicated when trying to generalize from Riemannian to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifolds"} Lorentzian manifolds
          %ul
            %li
              John K. Beem, Paul E. Ehrlich, Kevin L. Easley,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Global Lorentzian geometry
            %li
              John K. Beem,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lorentzian geometry in the large
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 41
              %a{:href => "http://matwbn.icm.edu.pl/ksiazki/bcp/bcp41/bcp4111.pdf"} pdf
          %p In particular, the conclusions of the Hopf-Rinow Theorem fail to hold for complete Lorentzian manifolds.
